// Which Dart entrypoint Xcode builds for RELEASE and PROFILE — which is what
// Product ▸ Archive and `flutter build ipa` use, i.e. what goes to the App
// Store and TestFlight. Pinned to PROD on purpose and not meant to be edited:
// pointing it at dev once (to run dev from Xcode) is exactly how a store
// build shipped talking to https://localhost:7199.
//
// Debug builds (Run from Xcode, `flutter run`) read Flavor.dev.xcconfig
// instead — change that one to run another flavor while developing.
//
// Why a pin at all: Flutter writes FLUTTER_TARGET into Generated.xcconfig from
// the last `flutter run` / `flutter build`, and Xcode never rewrites it, so an
// Archive started from Xcode would silently inherit whichever flavor the last
// command line used. This file is included AFTER Generated.xcconfig, and in an
// xcconfig the last assignment wins.

FLUTTER_TARGET = lib/flavors/main_prod.dart
